					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13486040#post-4712024</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13486040/in-memoria-adytum#post-4712024</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 07 Jul 2020 08:34:26 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Wakawaaa</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>5578352</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Well I'm always on the lookout for new cannons. It's the easiest way to engage in a fully told story on this wiki. Of course even the best of cannons tend to spill out, but that's not really a bad thing. This one seems a bit concerning though, the absolute scale of content to do with Sarkicism on the wiki threatens to make a cannon based on their story susceptible to many misunderstandings, with new authors for the cannon eager to refrence their favorite Sarkic stories. I can think of a few stories like that off the top of my head that would be pretty antithetical to the point of this cannon, but for now this hasn't happened.</p> <p>Who am I to judge though? I've no experience with the daunting challenge of managing a cannon. I'll be back.</p> <p>All can be good in the world.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
